    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = x+yx^{2}, \left(1,-2\right), \left(1,2\right), \left(-1,3\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(1,-2\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(1,2\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-1,3\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(1,-2\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(1,-2) = 1   - 2(1)^{2} = -1</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(1,2\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(1,2) = 1  + 2(1)^{2} = 3</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(-1,3\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-1,3) = -1  + 3(-1)^{2} = 2</m>.


</solution>
